      "title": "Error budget status \u2014 every SLO in the platform",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "One row per SLO: the objective Sloth was given, the SLI right now, how much of the 30-day budget survives, and how fast it is going.\n\nBurn rate is the column to read first \u2014 it is coloured at the alert thresholds (1x sustainable, 6x and 14.4x the two page conditions). Budget remaining is the column to act on: a service at 14x with 80% of its budget left has hours of headroom, and one at 2x with 3% left does not. The two together are the whole error-budget conversation.\n\nValues come from Sloth's meta recording rules, so they are the same numbers the alerting rules evaluate \u2014 not a re-derivation that could drift from them.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "custom": {
            "align": "auto",
            "cellOptions": {
              "type": "auto"
            },
            "filterable": false,
            "inspect": false
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "SLO"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.width",
                "value": 260
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
