      "title": "Current burn rate (5m) \u2014 all SLOs",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "description": "Six SLOs, one axis, because burn rate is already normalised by each SLO's own error budget \u2014 a 14.4 on recs and a 14.4 on catalog are the same statement about urgency even though catalog's budget is ten times smaller. That is the entire reason to plot burn rate rather than error ratios here.\n\nDashed lines: 1x sustainable, 6x and 14.4x the page thresholds. This is the 5m window only, so it moves first and is the leading edge of an incident; the page also requires its long-window partner (1h or 6h) below to agree.\n\nSeveral services above 1x at once points at something shared \u2014 the node, the network, a chaos experiment \u2014 rather than at any one service."
    },
